'''''[[Strictly Come Dancing]]''''' returned for its '''thirteenth series''' on [[BBC One]] with a launch show on 5 September 2015,<ref name="Launch">{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/proginfo/2015/36/strictly-come-dancing-the-launch-show|title=Strictly Come Dancing – The Launch Show|date=20 August 2015|publisher=[[BBC]]|accessdate=20 August 2015}}</ref> and the live shows beginning on 25 September 2015.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/showsandtours/shows/strictly_2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150830000049/http://www.bbc.co.uk/showsandtours/shows/strictly_2015|url-status=dead|archive-date=30 August 2015|title=BBC Shows and Tours – Shows – Strictly Come Dancing|publisher=BBC}}</ref> [[Tess Daly]] and [[Claudia Winkleman]] returned to present the launch show and the live shows<ref name="Launch"/> while [[Zoe Ball]] returned to present ''[[Strictly Come Dancing: It Takes Two]]'' on [[BBC Two]]. [[Darcey Bussell]], [[Len Goodman]], [[Craig Revel Horwood]], and [[Bruno Tonioli]] all returned as judges.<ref name="Launch"/>

[[The Wanted]] singer [[Jay McGuiness]] and [[Aliona Vilani]] were announced as the winners on 19 December, while [[Kellie Bright]] and [[Kevin Clifton]], and [[Georgia May Foote]] and [[Giovanni Pernice]] were the runners-up.

